{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782046070825,"sessionID":"ses_115c90015ffeGJZbxwLpcjHeWS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_5a35b90e217d4c6a8af07be9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"spring.datasource.url=jdbc:sqlite:file::memory:?cache=shared\nspring.datasource.driver-class-name=org.sqlite.JDBC\nspring.sql.init.mode=always\nspring.datasource.hikari.maximum-pool-size=1\n","filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-e2f7716088a3/src/test/resources/application-test.properties"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-z0i76flh/retort-e2f7716088a3/src/test/resources/application-test.properties","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"src/test/resources/application-test.properties","time":{"start":1782046070819,"end":1782046070824}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me make sure spring.sql.init runs schema.sql for in-memory SQLite. Spring Boot runs schema.sql automatically when spring.sql.init.mode=always. Good.\n\nBut there's a concern: with SQLite in-memory `jdbc:sqlite::memory:`, each connection gets its own database. Spring's HikariCP pools connections, so the schema created on one connection might not be visible on another. Actually for SQLite `:memory:`, the database is per-connection. This could break tests because schema.sql runs on one connection and queries run on another.\n\nBetter to use a file-based test DB or use SQLite shared memory mode. SQLite supports `jdbc:sqlite:file::memory:?cache=shared`. Let me update test properties to use shared in-memory.\n\nActually with HikariCP, the safer approach is to set the pool max-size to 1, or use a file. Let me use a file under target/ for tests, or use shared cache. Let me use shared cache with the proper URL format.\n\nThe xerial sqlite-jdbc driver supports `jdbc:sqlite::memory:?cache=shared` or `jdbc:sqlite:file::memory:?cache=shared`. With cache=shared, multiple connections share the same in-memory DB as long as at least one connection keeps it alive. With HikariCP pool keeping connections open, it should persist.\n\nLet me set spring.datasource.hikari.maximum-pool-size=1 to be safe for tests.\n\nActually simpler: use a file db in target dir that gets recreated. Let me just use a file path that's unique per test run. But that leaves files. Let me use shared memory + max-pool-size=1.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_eea39181f001WU2PZC8a15ZMGQ","sessionID":"ses_115c90015ffeGJZbxwLpcjHeWS","messageID":"msg_eea38f37b001LjoQr9XEf01Vom"}}
