{"type":"text","timestamp":1782046161026,"sessionID":"ses_115c90015ffeGJZbxwLpcjHeWS","part":{"id":"prt_eea3a6c8b001yG7bj4w2UUObF1","messageID":"msg_eea3a58750019SyBaYmbca6Pch","sessionID":"ses_115c90015ffeGJZbxwLpcjHeWS","type":"text","text":"Done. The Books REST API is implemented in Java with Spring Boot + SQLite, and builds cleanly with all tests passing.\n\n**What was built:**\n- **Endpoints:** `POST/GET/PUT/DELETE /books`, `GET /books?author=`, `GET /books/{id}`, `GET /health`\n- **Persistence:** SQLite via `sqlite-jdbc` + Spring `JdbcTemplate`; schema auto-created from `schema.sql`\n- **Validation:** `@NotBlank` on `title`/`author` → `400 Bad Request`\n- **Status codes:** `201` create, `200`/`204`/`400`/`404` as appropriate\n- **Tests (12, all passing):**\n  - `BookApiIntegrationTest` — full create/list/filter/get/update/delete flow over MockMvc, health check, validation failure, 404 handling (in-memory SQLite)\n  - `BookServiceTest` — 8 service-layer unit tests using a hand-rolled fake repository (avoided Mockito since it doesn't yet support Java 26 in this env)\n\nRun with `mvn spring-boot:run` (or `./mvnw spring-boot:run`). See `README.md` for full setup and API usage.","time":{"start":1782046157963,"end":1782046161025}}}
